# pip-audit Known Vulnerability Exceptions
#
# This file documents known vulnerabilities that cannot be resolved
# due to transitive dependency constraints or lack of available fixes.
#
# Format: One CVE per line with justification and re-review date
#
# CVE-ID | Package | Affected Versions | Justification | Re-review Date
#
# Example:
# CVE-2023-12345 | package-name | >=1.0,<2.0 | No fix available upstream. Risk accepted as... | 2025-06-01

# diskcache CVE-2025-69872
# Risk: Attacker with write access to cache directory can execute arbitrary code
# Mitigation: Cache directory is owned by the same user running the application.
# Victor uses diskcache for local caching only, not shared caches.
# Waiting for upstream fix or alternative caching library.
CVE-2025-69872 | diskcache | 5.6.3 | No newer version available. Vulnerability requires attacker write access to cache directory. In Victor's use case, cache directory is owned by application user. Acceptable risk for local caching. Re-evaluate when diskcache 5.7+ is released. | 2025-07-01

# PYSEC-2026-2447 is the OSV/PYSEC alias of the diskcache advisory accepted
# above as CVE-2025-69872 (pip-audit began reporting the PYSEC id). Same
# assessment: requires attacker write access to the cache directory; Victor
# uses diskcache for single-user local caching only. No fixed release yet.
PYSEC-2026-2447 | diskcache | 5.6.3 | Alias of CVE-2025-69872 (accepted above). No fix released. Local single-user cache; attacker needs cache-dir write access. Re-evaluate when diskcache >5.6.3 is released. | 2026-11-01
